      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-30T17:37:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e When running the test cases do the simulator and fpsensor get initialized once at startup\n\nFpsensor and fingerprint simulator are initialized once at startup.\n\nThe simulator has nothing to initialize really, and we can change the simulator state from test.\n\nManipulating the state of the fpsensor task is difficult because I can influence it using host commands, the simulator, and algorithm mock. This becomes a problem when I have tests that initializes TPM seed (we can\u0027t deinitialize TPM seed).\n\nYour suggestion is good. I\u0027ll update this CL, it\u0027s not a problem.",
      "parentUuid": "75630872_62cff9dc",
